# Normalise line endings in text, and never let git touch a board.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.js   text eol=lf
*.css  text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# .mbrd is a renamed ZIP - binary, and a diff of it is meaningless.
*.mbrd binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mp3  binary
# Vendored WebAssembly, and the one entry here that is not about a diff. The
# rule at the top is text=auto, which decides by sniffing - and a build that
# sniffed wrong would be checked out with its line endings rewritten and would
# no longer be a wasm module. tests/occt-vendor.test.js checks the magic number
# for that reason; this is what stops it happening.
*.wasm binary

# What the source zip leaves out. Each release carries `git archive` of its
# commit (research/apps-2026-09-13.md #32), and the repository is private for
# the sake of the plans and notes, not the code. The specs under research/docs/
# describe the file format the app writes, so they go in. Name each folder
# rather than research/** with an exception: git archive drops a matched
# folder whole, so an exception under it is never read.
research/*.md    export-ignore
research/old     export-ignore
research/future  export-ignore
scratch          export-ignore
CLAUDE.md        export-ignore
